{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And these are the garments that they shall make.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Arakhin: just as the sacrifices atone, so too the priestly garments atone; and therefore the passage of the sacrifices was juxtaposed to the passage of the priestly garments. The choshen atones for the judges, as it is said (Exodus 28): ״ועשית חשן משפט״. The ephod atones for idolatry, as it is said (Hosea 3:4): ״ואין אפוד ותרפים״, and it is written (Judges 8:27): ״ויעש אותו גדעון לאפוד״. The me'il atones for evil speech, as it is said (Exodus 28): ״ונשמע קולו״ — let the thing of sound come and atone for the deed of sound; and this evil speech is evil speech in public, but evil speech in private — the incense atones for it. The kethonnet tashbeitz atones for the shedding of blood, as it is said (Genesis 37:31): ״ויטבלו את הכתנת בדם״; and this kethonnet was like a tunic and was worn close to his flesh, and woven with gold, like a tunic upon which they embroider stripes, and so it is written (Exodus 28): ״ושבצת הכתנת שש״, from the expression of ״משבצות זהב״. The mitznephet atones for the arrogant — let the thing of height come and atone for the deed of height; and the avnet atones for the thoughts of the heart, and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that the avnet was thirty-two cubits. The tzitz atones for brazenness, as it is said (Exodus 28): ״והיה על מצח אהרן״, and it is written (Jeremiah 3:3): ״ומצח אשה זונה היה לך״. And the garments of the High Priest were eight, and Scripture mentioned six of them, and did not mention the tzitz because it is a golden vessel and is not included among the garments, and did not mention the linen breeches (מכנסי הבד), because he wished to mention only the six that Moses would put on Aaron; therefore he mentioned them together in this verse, as it is written at the end of the parashah: ״והלבשת את אהרן״ etc., and it is written after it: ״ועשה להם מכנסי בד״, to make clear that the breeches were what they put on themselves in private — so that you should not understand that the breeches were included [in the garments of which Moses dressed Aaron]; and therefore והלבשת was of necessity mentioned at the end, and it was impossible to include them together with the rest of the garments. And the breeaches (מכנסים) atone for immorality and for the walking of the feet that go to commit a transgression."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya writes ל״ב אמות (32 cubits) for the avnet, following the talmudic tradition; digit preserved exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:08.007739112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}